  clock: 3  # 9f86
  nonce: 9f86  # 9f86
  message: "Fixed (bundled PR, merged as abd9b2dd65). Root cause: Limits.to_dict wrote test_files_excluded into output only when True, and no production path ever sets it True, so the key was always absent — absence indistinguishable from 'tests included' (the only state production produces). Fix: always emit test_files_excluded as its actual bool, so the state is observable (false when not excluded, true if a future exclusion path sets it). Behavioral evidence: Limits().to_dict()['test_files_excluded'] is False (was: key absent); the True case still emits True. Schema: moved out of the conditional set (always present); regenerated docs/schema.json; test_limits_def_matches_to_dict updated to populate the now-conditional partial_results_reason. Test: test_test_files_excluded_present_false_when_not_excluded (rewrote the old not-in-output-when-false test to the new observable contract). 100% coverage."  # 9f86
